    "language": "en",
    "statementMarkdown": "We are given a collection of $2^{2^{k}}$ coins, where $k$ is a non-negative integer. Exactly one coin is fake. We have an unlimited number of service dogs. One dog is sick but we do not know which one. A test consists of three steps: select some coins from the collection of all coins; choose a service dog; the dog smells all of the selected coins at once. A healthy dog will bark if and only if the fake coin is amongst them. Whether the sick dog will bark or not is random.\n\nDevise a strategy to find the fake coin, using at most $2^{k}+k+2$ tests, and prove that it works.\n",
    "rawSha256": "2e4584eddc53593601137539b97a77a192a7020511c8fd1ce7515241733e1a09",
